<title>NETHERLANDS: UK FUND MANAGER SUSPENDED IN POACHING ROW - FT.</title>
<headline>UK FUND MANAGER SUSPENDED IN POACHING ROW - FT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>One of the most powerful fund managers in the City of London was suspended on Tuesday pending a probe into allegations she tried to lure colleagues at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell to move with her to ABN AMRO, the Financial Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Nicola Horlick had been suspended by Morgan Grenfell Asset Management, which is owned by Germany's Deutsche Bank, &quot;pending an internal investigation into what we think might be a breach of her contract&quot;, the paper quoted MGAM chief executive Robert Smith as saying.</p>
<p>Dutch ABN AMRO has been building up its fund management and other operations in London. The FT said the group, for whom hiring Horlick would be an enormous coup, declined comment.</p>
